ntermediate"><addressbook><name>OMRON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, SHINYA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI MASATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASAI KEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITOH SHIN-ICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA SHINYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAI, KEI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITOH, SHIN-ICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, SHINYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A liquid spray device, wherein a spray chamber (10C) is provided at one part of a device housing (1) and a liquid feeding mechanism (30) is provided at the other part thereof, at least either of ultrasonic vibrators (20, 21) is disposed inside the spray chamber and a liquid feeding hole (16) is provided in a part of the wall of the spray chamber, a liquid bottle (90) having a minute hole (91) at the tip thereof and a movable piston (93) installed therein can be installed at one end of the liquid feeding mechanism which can be positioned so that the minute hole in the liquid bottle installed in the liquid feeding mechanism is aligned with a liquid feeding hole formed in the spray chamber, and the liquid feeding mechanism comprises a manual operating member (40) and pressing mechanisms (50, 60) which move forward the piston in the installed liquid bottle by a specified stroke when the manual operating member is operated.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif pulvérisateur de liquide. La chambre de pulvérisation (10C) est logée dans une partie du boîtier (1) du dispositif et un mécanisme doseur de liquide dans l'autre partie. Au moins deux vibreurs ultrasoniques (20, 21) sont placés à l'intérieur de la chambre de pulvérisation. Une partie de la paroi de ladite chambre comporte un orifice doseur de liquide (16). Une bouteille (90) de liquide, pourvue d'un petit orifice (91) pratiqué à son extrémité et un piston (93) mobile placé dans cet orifice, peut être installée à une extrémité du mécanisme doseur de liquide, lequel peut être positionné de façon à aligner ledit petit orifice avec l'orifice doseur de la chambre de pulvérisation. Le mécanisme doseur de liquide comprend un élément de fonctionnement manuel (40) et des mécanismes de pression (50, 60) qui entraînent le piston en avant, dans la bouteille de liquide installée, d'une course spécifiée lorsqu'on actionne l'élément de fonctionnement manuel.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>